- *V.S. Sukthankar:* Leader of the Mahabharata Critical Edition project (1919--1966).
- *Patriliny:* Tracing descent and inheritance from father to son (*pitrivamsha*).
- *Endogamy:* Marriage practice of seeking a spouse within one's own kin group or locality.
- *Exogamy:* Marriage practice of seeking a spouse outside one's kin group/gotra.
- *Polyandry:* Marital arrangement where one woman has several husbands (e.g., Draupadi).
- *Polygyny:* Marital arrangement where one man has several wives (e.g., Satavahana kings).
- *Gotra:* Exogamous clan lineage named after a Vedic rishi, formulated c. 1000 BCE.
- *Matronymic:* Name derived from that of the mother (e.g., Gautamiputra).
- *Stridhana:* Woman's bridal wealth gifted at marriage, exempt from husband's division.
- *Mahasammata:* "The great chosen one", first contractual monarch in Buddhist political mythology.

